## How to Run Locally

```bash
# Install dependencies
npm install

# Start dev server
npm run dev

# Build for production
npm run build
```

---

## Deployment (Vercel — recommended)

1. Push project to a GitHub repo
2. Go to vercel.com → New Project → Import the repo
3. Vercel auto-detects Astro — no config needed
4. Every push to `main` triggers a new deploy automatically
5. Add a custom domain (e.g. `ektawedsajay.com`) in Vercel project settings

---

## Notes

- All interactive sections (Countdown, RSVP, Updates) are Astro islands — only they ship JS to the browser
- Rest of the site is pure HTML — extremely fast first load
- Fully responsive — mobile-first Tailwind layout
- Respects `prefers-reduced-motion` — GSAP animations are skipped if user has this enabled
- No backend or database — static site, zero running costs